    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d88-a7">

                <pb facs="0244" n="186" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg186"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 7.</seg></opener>
                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <p rendition="#center">MEXICAN REPUBLIC—ADVANCED STATION, NEAR TLACOTALPAM.</p>
                <p>At eleven at night my forces were in front of Tlacotalpam, about to begin the
                    attack, when the gunboats opened upon us, and we were compelled to retire. They
                    are now on the surrounding heights, determined to annoy the garrison as long as
                    possible.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Independence and liberty! Camp at
                            <placeName>Amates</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1866-05-29">May 29, 1866</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>F. CARREON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">General Second in Chief</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of the Eastern Line</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
